// D1690 — a DECLARED inline-shape row that nothing constructs captures an anonymous
// union-box literal, and the payload is then read against that row's tags. The value under
// test boxes `i32 | boolean` and holds the i32 `7`; the prelude's `type H` boxes
// `string | boolean`, whose tag 1 is `boolean`, so the capture prints `true`.
//
// This template is graded by PRINTED VALUE, not by whether the cell builds: every red cell
// here is a check-clean WRONG VALUE, which is why `WANT` is `7` and not a run marker.
//
// `type H` is never named by a value. Declaring it is the whole ingredient — an uncalled
// function's parameter annotation does the same job — so nothing in the prelude is called.
//
// The ANNOTATED face pins the literal to its own two-member shape and must keep printing `7`;
// the un-annotated face is the defect. The widening control lives in the fixture
// `tests/cases/structs/anon-struct-declared-box-row-not-captured.vl`, not here: a declared box
// field WIDER than the value's own union must keep accepting the literal, which is what makes
// this a preference rather than a refutation.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type U1 = i32 | boolean
type U2 = string | boolean
type H = { xs: U2 }
function u1(): U1 { return 7 }
function u1b(): U1 { return 8 }
// @@VALUE@@
{ xs: u1() }
// @@TYPE@@
{ xs: U1 }
// @@PROOF@@
print(v.xs)
// @@WANT@@
7
// @@VALUE2@@
{ xs: u1b() }
// @@TYPE2@@
{ xs: U1 }
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v.xs)
// @@WANT2@@
8
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a struct, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
